{"game": "back-4-blood", "language": "english", "appid": 924970, "month": "2023-06", "window": 3, "start_date": 1686873600, "end_date": 1687564799, "month_true_total": 178, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-08-29 20:50:36 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "140581516", "author": {"steamid": "76561198054536169", "personaname": "Prowo", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/penguin831/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 9, "playtime_forever": 3525, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3525, "last_played": 1687559429, "avatar": "5c8b6616a4d7c8b31bc25f70746e9d0f0ac21559"}, "language": "english", "review": "Man, I got this game from the humble bundle for cheap. I want to like this game so much, but as it stands I cannot. The overall gameplay is fun for the first time, but attempting the game solo in No Hope theres a lot of glaring issues. The bots are really bad, the fact the run in front of you when you shoot is the most frustrating thing ever and just bad AI in general. I cant play online without people leaving and one loss. You will think after the game was done after 1 year of content that they would fix some bugs that just give you an instant loss. \n\nI have played online and experienced the DLC. Its fun content and new cards, characters, and map add some much more gameplay. But the game barely feels finished after 1 year of content. TRT left with disappointment and used their one hit wonder to sell this game as AAA. If only they left with mod support and provided custom gamemodes so I dont have to play with bad RNG, weird bugs, and barebone card system.\n\nI enjoyed my first play through and online matches. I loved to make class specific decks, but the constant mix on unpolishness made me not recommend this game unless its your first zombie game or need to scratch that itch.\n\n6/10", "timestamp_created": 1687559933, "timestamp_updated": 1687559933, "voted_up": false, "votes_u